### Get all users
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users

###

### Get user by ID
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users/1

###

### Create a user
POST http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rahul Kumar",
  "email": "rahul@example.com",
  "address": "Bangalore, Karnataka",
  "password": "YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE",
  "role": "USER"
}



### 1. Get All Users
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users

###

### 2. Get User By ID
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users/3

###

### 3. Search Users
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users?search=Rahul

###

### 4. Filter Users By Role
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users?role=USER

###

### 5. Pagination
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users?page=1&limit=2

###

### 6. Sort Users By Name
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users?sortBy=name&order=asc

###

### 7. Invalid User ID
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/users/9999

###

